@{
    // Element 7: what a plan change actually means for the publisher. Renders bare.
    //
    // Deliberately does NOT state proration or refund mechanics. Those are Microsoft's billing
    // behaviour and are not documented in the fulfillment reference, so asserting them in a
    // teaching sample would be inventing detail.
}
<h3 class="learn-h">@L["What a plan change means for you"]</h3>
<div class="pc-figure" role="img" aria-label="@L["One subscription before the change, one after — only the plan differs."]">
    <div class="pc-box">
        <span class="pc-cap">@L["Before"]</span>
        <code>sub-0001</code>
        <span class="pc-plan">plan: <code>silver</code></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pc-arrow">
        <span class="pc-arrow-line" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
        <span class="pc-arrow-lbl">@L["ChangePlan webhook"]</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pc-box">
        <span class="pc-cap">@L["After"]</span>
        <code>sub-0001</code>
        <span class="pc-plan">plan: <code>gold</code></span>
    </div>
</div>
<ul class="pc-points">
    <li>@L["Still one subscription — same id. A plan change is an update, not a new purchase."]</li>
    <li>@L["Only an active subscription can change plan, and it stays active throughout."]</li>
    <li>@L["Your job: switch the features, then answer the Operations API within 10 seconds."]</li>
    <li>@L["Pricing and invoicing stay on Microsoft's side. This app never calculates money."]</li>
</ul>
<p class="learn-foot">
    @L["Try it: change the plan in the emulator and watch the plan, provenance and allowance move together."]
    <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/marketplace-offers/pc-saas-fulfillment-life-cycle" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@L["Lifecycle reference"]</a>,
    <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/marketplace-offers/pc-saas-fulfillment-operations-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@L["Operations API reference"]</a>.
</p>
